---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/site';

const principles = [
  {
    title: 'Transparent',
    body: 'Every result shows its work: the caps, thresholds, and phase-out steps behind the number, so you can check it against the law yourself.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Private by design',
    body: 'Our calculators run entirely in your browser. The figures you enter are never sent to or stored on our servers.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Free and independent',
    body: 'We are supported by advertising, not by selling your data or upselling tax products. No sign-up is ever required.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us"
  description="NetWageTax builds free, transparent, client-side paycheck and workplace tax calculators for American workers. Learn about our mission and how we work."
>
  <div class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">About NetWageTax</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
        We build free, transparent calculators that help American workers understand their paychecks and the tax rules
        that shape them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h2 id="mission">Our mission</h2>
    <p>
      Tax rules that affect everyday workers, such as how tips are taxed, how overtime is treated, or what a new code
      on your W-2 means, are often explained in dense legal language or buried behind paid software. NetWageTax exists
      to close that gap. Our goal is to give every worker clear, accurate, and free answers to the paycheck and
      workplace tax questions they actually have.
    </p>
    <p>
      We focus on the moments that matter: when a new law changes what you can deduct, when a form shows up with an
      unfamiliar box, or when you want to know what a raise or extra shift really means for your take-home pay.
    </p>

    <h2 id="principles">What we stand for</h2>
    <ul class="!list-none !pl-0 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
      {
        principles.map(({ title, body }) => (
          <li class="!mt-0 rounded-xl bg-white p-5 ring-1 ring-slate-200">
            <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">{title}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">{body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <h2 id="how">How we build our calculators</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Primary sources first.</strong> Our tools are built from statutory text, IRS forms and instructions,
        and official guidance, not from secondhand summaries.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Tested logic.</strong> Calculation engines are covered by automated tests for caps, filing statuses,
        and phase-out edge cases before they go live.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Kept current.</strong> Tax parameters are stored by tax year so they can be updated when the IRS
        publishes new figures or guidance.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Honest about limits.</strong> We tell you what a tool does not cover, such as FICA or state taxes, so an
        estimate is never mistaken for a final answer.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="tools">Our tools</h2>
    <p>
      Our first calculator, the <a href="/tools/obbba-tax-calculator">2026 OBBBA Tips &amp; Overtime Calculator</a>,
      estimates the new federal deductions for qualified tips and overtime created by the One Big Beautiful Bill Act,
      and decodes the new W-2 Box 12 Codes TA, TP, and TT. We are expanding our library of paycheck and withholding
      tools over time.
    </p>

    <h2 id="independence">Independence and funding</h2>
    <p>
      NetWageTax is an independent project. We are not affiliated with the IRS, any government agency, any employer,
      or any tax preparation company. The Site is funded by advertising, and advertisers have no influence over our
      calculations or content. NetWageTax is an educational tool and not a substitute for a qualified tax
      professional. Please read our <a href="/disclaimer">Financial &amp; Tax Disclaimer</a> for details.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Found an error, have a question, or want to suggest a calculator? Email us at 
      <a href={` mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We read every message, although we cannot provide
      individual tax advice.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
